{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/185026-blood-smoke-daysleep-and-waking","id":185026,"title":"Blood & Smoke - Daysleep and Waking","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-30T13:37:59-07:00","id":185026,"title":"Blood & Smoke - Daysleep and Waking","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I\u2019m new to the forum, so hi y\u2019all!</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Also, I\u2019m not an english native speaker, so this could result in some broken english and spaghetti.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I have a question about the Blood &amp; Smoke daysleep and waking rules.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">On B&amp;S, page 98 it states: </span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>When something disturbs the vampire\u2019s slumber or puts her at risk, make a Stamina + Resolve roll. Success allows her to remain awake for a number of turns equal to her Humanity. Failure means she remains asleep. Once those turns are over, she falls back to sleep without an additional Humanity roll. Once she\u2019s exceeded 5 + her Blood Potency successes during her waking turns, she can remain awake indefinitely, as if she never went to sleep in the first place.</i> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">To me, it\u2019s not completely clear what the \u201c<i>exceeding X successes</i>\u201d part is referring to. Does it mean that I have to roll Stamina + Resolve each turn I can remain awake (equal to my Humanity) and try to exceed 5 + BP successes with these rolls? Or I can try to exceed the successes with every roll I make while I\u2019m awake (for example, finding an intruder, combat\u2026 and each success I score counts towards the goal)?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Thx for the answers!</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3401-uata","name":"Uata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T14:04:18-07:00","id":185044,"title":"","content":"Hi, welcome to the forum.<br /> <br /> First, you might want to go to DriveThruRPG and download the updated PDF. Stamina + Resolve in the quote above was an error; it should actually be a Humanity roll.<br /> <br /> After you've been up for [Humanity] turns, you can either choose to go back to sleep or make a Humanity roll. Success on this roll allows you to stay up another [Humanity] turns. Once your total successes (on <i>all</i> of your awakeness-related Humanity rolls this day) exceeds [5 + Blood Potency], you can stay awake for the rest of the day with no additional rolls.<br /> <br /> I hope that helps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T14:07:16-07:00","id":185046,"title":"","content":"You still take the Lethargic Condition if you do that, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T14:14:13-07:00","id":185050,"title":"","content":"Many thanks ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3401-uata","name":"Uata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T11:12:23-07:00","id":894180,"title":"","content":"I am so lucky I found this thread. I couldn't figure out Rose's answer here from VTR 2nd Edition.<br /> I still want to ask a further question, though. The book says that waking and resisting daysleep are two totally different things mechanically. The former is rolled by Humanity (and doesn't give you the Lethargic condition) as described by Rose above, but the latter is a single Stamina + Resolve roll and gives you Lethargic unless you achieve an exceptional success. It is not that I don't understand the wording, I am just curious if these things are correct or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6216-p-czigany","name":"p.czigany","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T17:08:57-07:00","id":894438,"title":"","content":"Yes these are two different things.<br /> <br /> Waking up is one thing. You died for the day, now something is threatening you. You have a chance to roll to wake up while the sun is still up.<br /> <br /> Staying awake is another. The sun is coming up and you just dont want your night to end. You roll to stay awake and fight it. ( unless you roll exceptional) You have to keep rolling periodically or crash..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T02:23:22-07:00","id":894625,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Vitalis!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6216-p-czigany","name":"p.czigany","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}